WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.649 --> 00:00:03.360
- My comfort food is a
cheese dog, corned beef,

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:04.520
garlic rice with egg.

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:07.280
Let's cook it.

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:09.863
(upbeat music)

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:15.500
I learned how to cook
this meal, on my own,

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.570
growing up in the Philippines.

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:20.250
Probably around 8 to 10 years old.

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:23.930
I learned from just watching
family and relatives cook.

00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:28.110
It gives me joy because it
reminds me of the simpler times.

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:38.580
So, we got hot dogs,
looking for the cheese dogs.

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:41.100
I don't know if this is right

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:42.990
one, cause this one looks weird.

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:45.850
But it says its got cheese in it, so.

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:47.771
Corned beef, I used to think

00:00:47.771 --> 00:00:51.140
corned beef had some corn in it.

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:53.220
We got rice, whole lot of rice.

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:54.930
You could feed a whole family with this.

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:55.960
We got eggs,

00:00:57.180 --> 00:00:58.550
garlic,

00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:01.230
and onions for the rice and corned beef.

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:05.100
Of course, the secret
sauce, banana ketchup.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:14.580
First things first, rice.

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:20.740
You wash it because sometimes
it's a little dirty.

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:23.700
If you wanna measure it,
you just need your finger.

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:27.230
You measure the rice
first, and then after that,

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:30.680
you measure from the top
of the rice and the water

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:35.630
level should basically be
twice the height of the rice.

00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:36.740
Does that make sense?

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:40.320
That's it, and then you put it in here.

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:45.580
Turn it on, and we wait, it's like magic.

00:01:51.703 --> 00:01:53.703
(yells)

00:01:59.463 --> 00:02:02.582
It's for snaking a drain, I think.

00:02:02.582 --> 00:02:07.260
C'mon, c'mon, c'mon, c'mon, get it.

00:02:09.385 --> 00:02:12.145
(laughing)

00:02:12.145 --> 00:02:15.886
(victorious fanfare)

00:02:15.886 --> 00:02:17.316
- [Jake] You didn't
even start cooking yet.

00:02:17.316 --> 00:02:18.510
- Chop the onions.

00:02:20.825 --> 00:02:21.890
Yeah.

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:28.320
It's getting into my eyes.

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:29.153
Garlic.

00:02:33.922 --> 00:02:36.969
The corned beef, I like these cans cause,

00:02:36.969 --> 00:02:40.530
you just use a key and twist it.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:49.111
Looks kinda nasty but it tastes great.

00:02:49.111 --> 00:02:51.430
I'll pick this one.

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:56.387
So, I'm gonna put my corned beef.

00:02:56.387 --> 00:02:57.370
Look at that.

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:03.980
Just drop that in there, that's
too much, go back in there.

00:03:05.873 --> 00:03:07.270
Smush it up.

00:03:12.353 --> 00:03:13.603
What's in this?

00:03:14.890 --> 00:03:17.360
Just gonna put a couple for a meal.

00:03:19.353 --> 00:03:21.943
This is too big of a pan for this hot dog.

00:03:21.943 --> 00:03:24.943
(rice cooker beeps)

00:03:26.746 --> 00:03:28.330
Looks like rice.

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:34.840
In the Philippines, we have rice as

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:37.820
the base for any kind of meal.

00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:40.230
And everything else that you put on top

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:42.230
of rice is called, ulam.

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:45.190
Which is, the english
word for it is viand.

00:03:46.070 --> 00:03:47.096
I don't know what it means.

00:03:47.096 --> 00:03:47.929
- [Jake] What is it?

00:03:47.929 --> 00:03:50.560
- It's called viand, in Tagalog,

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:52.736
it's called ulam, which is everything

00:03:52.736 --> 00:03:56.360
else that you put on top of rice.

00:03:58.450 --> 00:03:59.990
Put these aside.

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:03.713
Hot dog.

00:04:04.570 --> 00:04:05.690
One hand.

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:12.690
Oh mother, oh.

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:17.230
Still full, that was lucky,
oh wait, this isn't on.

00:04:18.530 --> 00:04:22.160
Garlic, so now I'm gonna scoop some rice.

00:04:26.897 --> 00:04:29.627
Oh (bleep) that's hot.

00:04:29.627 --> 00:04:32.210
(sink running)

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:36.540
And that's about it.

00:04:39.908 --> 00:04:42.825
(harmonic singing)

00:04:43.890 --> 00:04:48.890
When I eat my comfort food,
I love to sit on the floor,

00:04:50.270 --> 00:04:53.260
by this coffee table on the edge, cause I

00:04:53.260 --> 00:04:57.090
can just lean on this
couch and watch the TV.

00:04:57.090 --> 00:05:00.840
You know when you have
that spot on the couch?

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:02.785
I have a spot on the floor.

00:05:02.785 --> 00:05:04.464
Try it.

00:05:04.464 --> 00:05:07.870
Here's the thing, I don't
know if that's a cheese dog.

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:13.100
- Good corned beef hash.

00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:15.990
- See if there's cheese inside.

00:05:17.070 --> 00:05:18.220
God (beep) it.

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:19.690
- I don't see cheese in there.

00:05:19.690 --> 00:05:23.120
- Wait, I was looking for
a hot dog with cheese,

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:27.488
little cheese dripping
down from the inside

00:05:27.488 --> 00:05:31.640
of it but, I chose the wrong one.

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:32.473
You like it?

00:05:32.473 --> 00:05:33.390
- I can see why it's comfort food,

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:35.390
very all comforting flavors.

00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:38.321
- You haven't tried it with
the banana ketchup, so this is.

00:05:38.321 --> 00:05:40.170
- I've never had banana ketchup.

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:41.080
- Just try it.

00:05:46.637 --> 00:05:47.470
How it it?

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:52.320
- It's like ketchup but
a little more acidic.

00:05:53.945 --> 00:05:54.990
- And sweet.

00:05:54.990 --> 00:05:55.860
- Sweet.

00:05:55.860 --> 00:05:57.890
- It's not what you
would think with banana.

00:05:57.890 --> 00:05:59.057
- It's not normal.
- Yeah.

00:05:59.057 --> 00:06:00.487
- I like banana ketchup.

00:06:00.487 --> 00:06:03.600
- Right, I love banana ketchup.

00:06:06.637 --> 00:06:08.160
You want it?

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:11.880
What this reminds me of, is my childhood

00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:15.710
and part of it is friends and relatives

00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:18.450
back in the Philippines, where we used

00:06:18.450 --> 00:06:20.972
to just run around, play outside.

00:06:20.972 --> 00:06:22.993
And also having to pray before

00:06:22.993 --> 00:06:25.490
every single meal with my family.

